  "notes": "The demolished Lyttelton Gaol in its late operating period. The Oxford Street Gothic entrance, principal cell ranges, yards and perimeter are the historical subject. The separate house across Oxford Street and the later Upham clock are outside scope. The present-day mapped legal boundary fixes the site envelope and surviving controls. Historic internal and building alignments are distinct estimates."
